{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>השבע השביע</b> — twice in the Masorah. The other: by Saul, <b>השבע השביע אביך את העם</b>. As we expound here: this teaches that he made his brothers swear that they would make their sons swear. There too, he made the people swear that they would make even those who were not present when he swore them swear. Therefore Jonathan was caught even though he did not hear the oath."], :book :exodus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {0 "The phrase השבע השביע אביך את העם is from 1 Samuel 14:27 (in context of Saul's oath); the verse address is not written by the author."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:12:45.609048408Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}